3.  THE ERROR BUDGET ON log alpha.  The measurement error is ONE term, and it is not the biggest
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  term                                                      delta gamma_v   -> dex in log alpha
  measurement (frozen sigma_tot = 0.028)                           0.0280                0.0644
  a0 FOOTING (canonical vs alt)                                    0.0170                0.0392
  g_ext convention (frozen primary vs alt)                         0.0094                0.0215
  eccentricity prior (thermal vs super-thermal)                    0.0077                0.0177
  semi-major-axis prior (log-uniform to 80 vs 25 kAU)              0.0016                0.0038
  mass calibration at 0.04 dex (eclipsing-binary MS relation)         0.0023                0.0053
  two-body composition convention (frozen 10(b))                   0.0475                0.1092
  frozen band width at fixed alpha (10(b) floor to top)            0.0200                0.0460
  TOTAL (quadrature)                                               0.0623                0.1434
  of which measurement 0.0644 dex and model systematics 0.1281 dex

  measured d log gamma_v / d log Upsilon (mass calibration) = -0.0227
  the candidate's own claim on this line is 'd log gamma_v/d log Upsilon = 0 EXACTLY on the PREDICTION
  side'.  That is TRUE for the asymptotic eigenvalues and FALSE for the sample-level prediction, because
  the mass sets h/g_ext and therefore which part of the transition each pair samples.
  [FAIL] 3a  THE CANDIDATE'S CENTRAL CLAIM: alpha is measurable to about 0.05 dex.  It survives only if the TOTAL budget -- not the measurement term alone -- is under 0.10 dex, i.e. within a factor 2 of the claim
         (total sigma(log alpha) = 0.1434 dex, of which 0.0644 is measurement and 0.1281 is model systematics.  The candidate quotes 0.0491 dex, the measurement term of the asymptotic map alone)
  [FAIL] 3b  CAN FAIL: is the measurement term the DOMINANT one, as the candidate's quoted precision assumes?
         (measurement 0.0644 dex vs systematics 0.1281 dex, a ratio of 2.0 the wrong way)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3c.  THE SAME FACT STATED WITHOUT ANY ERROR BUDGET: what alpha does the theory's OWN frozen band span?
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Amendment 10(b) registers gamma_v at alpha = 1 as a BAND, not a point, because the footing and the
  two-body composition convention are both unresolved.  Invert that band through this script's own
  sample-level map and read off the alpha interval it corresponds to:
    frozen canonical floor gamma_v = 1.1614  ->  alpha = 0.783
    frozen canonical top   gamma_v = 1.1814  ->  alpha = 0.743
    frozen alt       floor gamma_v = 1.1917  ->  alpha = 0.723
    frozen alt       top   gamma_v = 1.2267  ->  alpha = 0.659
    frozen per-star diagnostic canonical gamma_v = 1.1139  ->  alpha = 0.953
  READ ONLY, Amendment 10(c), verbatim: "DR4 separates the framework from Newton; it does NOT attribute
  the arm."  A statistic that cannot separate modified inertia from modified gravity is not going to
  separate alpha = 0.8 from alpha = 1.2 within the same arm.

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT -- K3 (alpha from the wide-binary boost)
======================================================================================================================
  1. THE CANDIDATE'S ARITHMETIC IS CORRECT.  Its asymptotic map and its lever (-0.537 / -0.570) are
     reproduced here to 3e-3.  NOT A RESTATEMENT: the deep-MOND relation is alpha-blind to 1e-8.
  2. THE SAMPLE-LEVEL LEVER IS WEAKER: -0.4348 against the asymptotic -0.5438, i.e. 76% retained,
     because the internal field, the orbit and the projection all dilute the alpha dependence.  The
     measurement-only precision is 0.064 dex, not the 0.049 dex quoted.
  3. THE MEASUREMENT ERROR IS NOT THE BUDGET.  Model systematics contribute 0.128 dex against the
     measurement's 0.064; the total is 0.143 dex.  The largest single term is
     'two-body composition convention (frozen 10(b))' at 0.109 dex.
  4. d log gamma_v / d log Upsilon = -0.0227 on the SAMPLE-LEVEL prediction, not 0.  Small, and
     genuinely the mildest mass lever in this hunt, but not the exact zero the candidate claims.
  5. THE THEORY'S OWN FROZEN BAND AT FIXED alpha = 1 IS WIDER THAN THE MEASUREMENT ERROR.  That is the
     decisive fact and it is not new here: it is registered in Amendment 10(b)-(c) and it is why the
     pre-registration says DR4 cannot even attribute the ARM.
  CATEGORY: FAILED as a Kepler-grade candidate -- criterion (3).  alpha is measurable in principle and
  the construction is sound; it is not measurable to 0.05 dex, and the block is not the data.

RESULT: 8 checks, 2 FAIL -> ["3a  THE CANDIDATE'S CENTRAL CLAIM: alpha is measurable to about 0.05 dex.  It survives only if the TOTAL budget -- not the measurement term alone -- is under 0.10 dex, i.e. within a factor 2 of the claim", "3b  CAN FAIL: is the measurement term the DOMINANT one, as the candidate's quoted precision assumes?"]
